cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you build on this software, findings, or ideas, please cite this repository and the exact commit used."
type: software
title: "FamilyTiles: Exact shared-weight representations for related language models"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/FamilyTiles"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/FamilyTiles"
abstract: >-
  Lossless residual encoding and Metal decoding for related BF16 checkpoints.
  The tested Qwen2.5-1.5B base/Instruct pair used 20.49 percent less active-
  weight representation storage with exact reconstruction. Custom model
  execution failed its numerical requirement and stock-operator fallbacks
  failed latency requirements; no validated memory-saving inference or
  physical process-peak reduction was demonstrated.
keywords:
  - language models
  - shared weights
  - lossless compression
  - BF16
  - Apple Silicon
  - Metal
  - negative results
